</section>
<section class="workflow" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="workflow-heading">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A practical starting point</p><h2 id="workflow-heading">Evidence in. Clear objectives out.</h2><p>Bring your subject knowledge. JBIDS keeps the sources, objectives, and decisions together.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature"><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Collect job evidence</h3><p>Save job announcements, their original links, and the full text. Keep the requirements available even when a listing disappears.</p></article>
        <article class="feature"><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Shape learning objectives</h3><p>Write measurable objectives, select a Bloom’s taxonomy level, and connect each objective to supporting excerpts from one or more announcements.</p></article>
        <article class="feature"><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Review with confidence</h3><p>Approve, reject, or refine each objective. When approved content or its evidence changes, it returns to Draft for a fresh review.</p></article>
    </div>
</section>
<section class="direction-panel" aria-labelledby="direction-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start focused. Build thoughtfully.</p><h2 id="direction-heading">A foundation for your curriculum.</h2><p>Today, collect evidence and review objectives. Future iterations will connect objectives to courses and degree plans, with LLM assistance and subject matter expert input.</p></div><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="/projects">Create your first project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
